WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.163
Before the slice runs, write the result you
expect, the metric, the date, and the evidence

00:00:05.233 --> 00:00:06.662
that would change your view.

00:00:06.732 --> 00:00:11.425
The prediction belongs to the experiment,
not a reconstructed success story.

00:00:11.495 --> 00:00:15.549
Establish a comparison baseline
with the same task definition.

00:00:15.619 --> 00:00:20.717
Evaluate rules before adding a model
so you can identify incremental value.

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:23.966
For this lab, functional
tests establish behavior.

00:00:24.036 --> 00:00:29.177
They do not establish reduced review time
until a timed task comparison occurs.

00:00:29.247 --> 00:00:35.157
You predict at most 14 minutes median review
time and no more than one misroute in twelve

00:00:35.227 --> 00:00:36.571
equivalent tasks.

00:00:36.641 --> 00:00:40.886
The lab test suite passes, but the
team has not timed any reviewers.

00:00:40.956 --> 00:00:43.793
These two evidence sets
answer different questions.

00:00:43.863 --> 00:00:48.642
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

00:00:48.712 --> 00:00:54.259
Write the prediction, run the tests, and state
exactly what a passing result establishes.

00:00:54.329 --> 00:01:00.899
Passing tests establish the specified local
API, validation, rule, audit, and approval

00:01:00.969 --> 00:01:07.860
behavior. They do not establish operator trust,
adoption, latency in a customer environment, or a causal

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:09.295
productivity gain.

00:01:09.365 --> 00:01:12.501
Keep the performance
prediction open until measured.

00:01:12.571 --> 00:01:19.078
An optional model comparison should reuse the
labeled evaluation set and include cost, errors,

00:01:19.148 --> 00:01:20.983
fallback, and review effort.

00:01:21.053 --> 00:01:24.978
Does a passing functional test
prove the outcome metric improved?

00:01:25.048 --> 00:01:26.989
A. Yes, automatically B.

00:01:27.059 --> 00:01:28.937
Only with a modern model C.

00:01:29.007 --> 00:01:31.161
No, outcome measurement is separate.

00:01:31.231 --> 00:01:32.639
The best answer is C.

00:01:32.709 --> 00:01:35.440
Match each claim to the
test that can establish it.
